{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum","id":1167409,"title":"Would you allow a Dice Adding spell with the Matter Arcanum.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-13T14:06:02-08:00","id":1167409,"title":"Would you allow a Dice Adding spell with the Matter Arcanum.","content":"My question is pretty much in the title, but let me clarify. <br /> <br /> Every time I go through the example matter spells, I am struck by the lack of spells that interact with or boost the equipment bonus of tools. There are lots of spells that apply dice tricks to your pool when you use spells (indeed so many it almost seems redundant), but nothing that can actually just add dice to your pool. Now clearly this isn't something the Mage writers felt no Mage should be able to accomplish, since Fate, Mind and Life can achieve dice adding relatively simply (through Boons and Skill/Attribute boosting respectively). <br /> <br /> Is there a reason why I shouldn't be able to use the Perfecting Practice of Matter to make a sword sharper and more deadly (increase its damage bonus) or make my laptop more efficient (increase its equipment bonus)? I only ask because the absence of such a spell feels almost intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T14:50:24-08:00","id":1167422,"title":"","content":"I don't see any problem with a spell like that.<br /> <br /> If you increase the bonus to a level higher than the normal max possible for that type of equipment (smartphones cap at +2, for example), than it might count as obvious magic to an expert in a field related to those devices, though, resulting in potential Dissonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T15:01:24-08:00","id":1167424,"title":"","content":"I suppose I could stick a Mana surcharge on such spells as well? Like when Life and Mind spells break the Attribute cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T15:16:21-08:00","id":1167428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1167424#post1167424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I could stick a Mana surcharge on such spells as well? Like when Life and Mind spells break the Attribute cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Equipment bonus is explicitly brought up in the Bonuses/Penalties subsection of the &quot;Determine Effect and Cost&quot; step of the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T16:49:40-08:00","id":1167447,"title":"","content":"I think the reason is that there's a very small window for the improvement of a tool before it has to change substantially. The difference between an standard and high quality needle is very small, and to really make the job easier you need a sewing machine. That's why I think the default spells opt for dice tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T03:27:04-08:00","id":1167556,"title":"","content":"Increasing equipment bonus with magic is allowed with creative thaumaturgy. A mage with Matter 3 could alter the Matter of a tool to make it better. For me, as long as the player could give at least a semi-flimsy justification, it would work. Obvious candidates are normal tools that would benefit from higher quality materials, like screwdrivers or most Physical equipment. Less obvious would be things like electronics. Altering the internal Matter of a computer to make it run faster isn't necessarily going to help you search the Internet better. But it might apply if you're using the computer to run simulations and crunch numbers.<br /> <br /> A creative thaumaturgy Matter 3 spell: Increase Equipment Bonus of the item by Potency. Good for a number of rolls equal to Potency. Going over the normal maximum, which I think is +3 for most Equipment, requires one point of Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T03:43:43-08:00","id":1167558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The \u201cTrait maximum\u201d for an equipment bonus is always +5. </div> </div> </div>Page 126 in the Bonus/Penalties section for dice numbers that can be manipulated via magic. Basically, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-14-2017, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T05:49:57-08:00","id":1167585,"title":"","content":"The way I handle it is that you can Perfect any equipment to any rating you want that is equal to or less than your Arcana Dots (or Potency, depending on how you handle similar spells; you could raise this an extra dot with reach).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T09:53:29-08:00","id":1174052,"title":"","content":"There's a prime spell for this and it diminishes the tool with each use so... for balance reasons I'd probably rule this it impossible to improve past +3. Prime already has so few effects it doesn't really need to have platonic objects taken from it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T10:02:22-08:00","id":1174055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174052#post1174052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a prime spell for this and it diminishes the tool with each use so... for balance reasons I'd probably rule this it impossible to improve past +3. Prime already has so few effects it doesn't really need to have platonic objects taken from it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there isn't. I assume you're referring to Platonic Form, but that creates something from mana rather than modifying an existing tool. This was a question about if Matter can do it, which there's no reason it can't since tools made of matter fall under its purview. There's also the fact that the book does specifically mention that equipment bonuses that are increased max out at five, not three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T10:17:06-08:00","id":1174063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174055#post1174055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, there isn't. I assume you're referring to Platonic Form, but that creates something from mana rather than modifying an existing tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semantic Difference.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174055#post1174055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was a question about if Matter can do it, which there's no reason it can't since tools made of matter fall under its purview. There's also the fact that the book does specifically mention that equipment bonuses that are increased max out at five, not three.</div> </div> </div> </div>To restate my reason to it's understood (whether or not you agree with it is up to you).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most equipment offers a bonus to dice rolls pertaining to its use. Multiple items can influence a given roll, but a roll should not receive more than a +5 bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me this is pretty simple. Matter can enhance mundane equipment to their natural peak. For most equipment this is +3 (with some exceptions). Enhancing them beyond that is no longer the purview of matter since you're attempting to create something that does not exist in the fallen world, which is the purview of Prime.<br /> <br /> Thus:<br /> I'd probably rule it is impossible to improve most items past +3. Prime already has so few effects that creating a functionally identical effect in matter breaches the meta-logic of having separate arcana to begin with, that you'll want to use them for different functions. Because ruling in favor of this weakens the scope of Prime via overlap, I would not allow it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","user":"Knit-I-Fine","date":". 01-07-2018, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T10:29:29-08:00","id":1174066,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2313_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2313\" data-vbnamecard=\"2313\">Knit-I-Fine</a> The book also has a section on using magic to increase traits on pg. 126 which I referenced earlier in this thread. A piece of equipment's bonus is considered a trait as per that section, and that section also says that that specific trait maximum is five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T10:37:55-08:00","id":1174067,"title":"","content":"I'm aware of that. It's still outside the purview of matter to make a thing that doesn't exist. There's no +5 tool for most skills, so matter magic cannot create one or transform a less effective tool into one. There is no frame of reference for such a thing outside the supernal so forming the imago for the spell would be impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T10:49:45-08:00","id":1174072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174067#post1174067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of that. It's still outside the purview of matter to make a thing that doesn't exist. There's no +5 tool for most skills, so matter magic cannot create one or transform a less effective tool into one. There is no frame of reference for such a thing outside the supernal so forming the imago for the spell would be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of examples of equipment with a +5 bonus doesn't mean they don't exist or can't be boosted to that level with Matter. One of the main uses of Perfecting is to make something draw closer to the Supernal ideal it's based on which is why traits can be increased with that Practice. This is especially true when the book flat out tells you that you can in fact do it.<br /> <br /> Also, it's well within Matter's purview to make things that don't exist, that's what the practice of Making is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T11:01:22-08:00","id":1174077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174072#post1174072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the main uses of Perfecting is to make something draw closer to the Supernal ideal it's based on which is why traits can be increased with that Practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's only so far you can draw something before you reach it's limit. An operating room grants a character a +3 equipment bonus to Medicine. At some point one has to remember that human beings are casting the spell, and in order to do so they have to envision the result. There's nothing to envision that grants +5 medicine.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why this is such a sticking point for you anyways since you can just use multiple tools to get up to that +5 bonus. Creating supernally perfect tools is prime, not matter.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174072#post1174072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of examples of equipment with a +5 bonus doesn't mean they don't exist or can't be boosted to that level with Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so now that I've established why a Mage can't just imagine a nonexistent medical tool that gives +5 medicine just because the game theoretically could stat one up we get to the only remaining point. Does a piece of equipment exist that grants a +5 bonus to Medicine? No. For most skills the answer is no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T11:25:53-08:00","id":1174084,"title":"","content":"The book explicitly states that an equipment bonus can hit +5, you're citing examples which don't hit that cap. The most obvious answer to me is that the examples you're citing are simply the average stats for those things. In other words, there do exist +5 operating rooms, but they're very uncommon and most are at best +3, magic can close that gap.<br /> <br /> Also, there is no reason to make perfect tools the sole purview of Prime, tools fall under Matter as well, and Matter and Prime both derive their power from manipulating the symbols of the Supernal. You're creating some weird partitioning in there that simply doesn't have any reason to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T11:41:40-08:00","id":1174092,"title":"","content":"It is a real partition between the arcana, it's called Purview. The Supernal World is not within Matter's purview, it is within Prime's purview (which is exceptionally narrow and so overlaps should be watched keenly). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The book says an equipment bonus' maximum is 5, sure. And that's useful if you're enhancing an item with Prime and need to know when you have to spend mana to go over the maximum, but it is not useful when trying to create real items.<br /> <br /> Are you familiar with hospitals and medicine? Like in real life, I'm just curious because that's why I've been using medicine as an example. There are not +5 operating rooms. Such a thing does not exist in the real world. There are three pieces of equipment in the core book that hit +5, they are a code kit, a gas mask, and a ridiculous amount of money. It's important to understand what that represents, these are items that essentially guarantee success in their use. There are few items that are that refined in the real world. If you want to add Time to Matter in order to try and pull a +5 object that hasn't been invented yet from the future, you're welcome to it, but magic can't create an item your character has no frame of reference for.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Basically, if there was a +5 item for everything, they would have set the bar a lot lower than they did with their examples. It's been made pretty clear +3 is standard topping out point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","user":"Knit-I-Fine","date":". 01-07-2018, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T17:01:20-08:00","id":1174151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174092#post1174092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a real partition between the arcana, it's called Purview. The Supernal World is not within Matter's purview, it is within Prime's purview (which is exceptionally narrow and so overlaps should be watched keenly). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Enhancing tools that already exist is under the purview of Matter, if there is an overlap with Prime then it's not a problem. There's a sidebar on page 124 titled Many Roads to this effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The book says an equipment bonus' maximum is 5, sure. And that's useful if you're enhancing an item with Prime and need to know when you have to spend mana to go over the maximum, but it is not useful when trying to create real items.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>You don't need Prime to enhance an object, or to spend Mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Are you familiar with hospitals and medicine? Like in real life, I'm just curious because that's why I've been using medicine as an example.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>My familiarity with hospitals and medicine has no bearing on the mechanics of the game as presented and is completely superfluous to the conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There are not +5 operating rooms. Such a thing does not exist in the real world.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be obvious that in the real world there isn't a +5 operating room because the real world doesn't deal with abstract bonuses to effectiveness, but it should be equally obvious that in the real world there are some operating rooms that are better equipped than others. The standard operating room according to the game is at +3, but that doesn't preclude the possibility of a better than standard operating room which could have a bonus of up to five.<br /> <br /> I do not need to imagine something I have no reference for, I need only imagine something that is better than the average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:05:41-08:00","id":1174166,"title":"","content":"Mrmdubois. You don't seem to have really understood what I've already said, so this is the last time I'm gonna address this topic. Making new tools that don't exist in the fallen world is outside of matters purview, so no, you cannot make an imaginary +5 medkit just because there is a +1 medkit, you can't make a +3 operating room just because an operating room provides a +3 bonus which isn't the <i>technical maximum that could ever be achieved in the fallen world by anything</i> or a a piece of duck tape into +5 ducktape because there isn't such a thing. To say otherwise is absurd to the point of parody and conjures up images of bat sharp repellent. That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:47:29-08:00","id":1174178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174166#post1174166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mrmdubois. You don't seem to have really understood what I've already said, so this is the last time I'm gonna address this topic. Making new tools that don't exist in the fallen world is outside of matters purview, so no, you cannot make an imaginary +5 medkit just because there is a +1 medkit, you can't make a +3 operating room just because an operating room provides a +3 bonus which isn't the <i>technical maximum that could ever be achieved in the fallen world by anything</i> or a a piece of duck tape into +5 ducktape because there isn't such a thing. To say otherwise is absurd to the point of parody and conjures up images of bat sharp repellent. That is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that you think that increasing a piece of equipment's bonus necessitates thinking up a new thing that could have that bonus. I'm saying that you don't need to do that, you just need to think of how that piece of equipment could be more effective and then apply a spell to it which gives it that level of effectiveness which in game terms means adding an equipment bonus.<br /> <br /> I'm also saying that the equipment given in the book is the standard, or average equipment of its kind, so it's entirely possible that there's a +5 medkit out there in the game world and a Mage with Matter is simply boosting his +1 kit to be as effective as that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-07-2018, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T19:28:02-08:00","id":1174192,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2313_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2313\" data-vbnamecard=\"2313\">Knit-I-Fine</a> In other words, I understand you perfectly, but I disagree with you, and I also think the rules disagree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T06:28:46-08:00","id":1174259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1167409-would-you-allow-a-dice-adding-spell-with-the-matter-arcanum?p=1174166#post1174166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mrmdubois. You don't seem to have really understood what I've already said, so this is the last time I'm gonna address this topic. Making new tools that don't exist in the fallen world is outside of matters purview, so no, you cannot make an imaginary +5 medkit just because there is a +1 medkit, you can't make a +3 operating room just because an operating room provides a +3 bonus which isn't the <i>technical maximum that could ever be achieved in the fallen world by anything</i> or a a piece of duck tape into +5 ducktape because there isn't such a thing. To say otherwise is absurd to the point of parody and conjures up images of bat sharp repellent. That is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic is about doing things that are impossible, it's funny like that.<br /> <br /> Matter can also cause water to run uphill, something that could not happen and is just absurd. It can also make you invisible to cameras, which shouldn't be able to happen in reality. Or it can create materials out of nothing, which completely violates all physical laws in existence.<br /> <br /> You could also cause a person to exceed <i>the human maximum </i>in all of the Attributes and Skills using magic. Would you ban those spells as well because they don't conform to reality?<br /> <br /> No, I wouldn't allow +5 medikits or smartphones either to exist as mundanely created items by normal mortals. With magic though? Yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 01-08-2018, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}